============================================================================================
4+2 PACKET: (1,1,1,1,a,a)
============================================================================================
Square shells are conjugate frequency pairs {m,-m}, indexed by m^2 in F_7^*.  For the non-identity 4+2 row these shells are sign-definite, so the shell bound equals the signed mass while still exposing chi_7(a).

 a  chi      S/U    |S|/U   chiBd/U   sqBd/U   blind/u        square shells q=1,2,4
 1    1        0    0.000     0.000    0.000    48.698                  1:0 2:0 4:0
 2    1      -25   25.000    25.000   25.000    34.215               1:0 2:-9 4:-16
 3   -1      -18   18.000    18.000   18.000    31.725                1:-9 2:0 4:-9
 4    1      -25   25.000    25.000   25.000    36.243               1:-9 2:-16 4:0
 5   -1      -18   18.000    18.000   18.000    30.302                1:-9 2:-9 4:0
 6   -1      -18   18.000    18.000   18.000    38.108               1:-2 2:0 4:-16

Punctured character law for a in {2,3,4,5,6}:
  2*S(1,1,1,1,a,a)/U = -43 - 7*chi_7(a)
  equivalently |S|/U = (43 + 7*chi_7(a))/2.
This is the QR/NQR split HYP-2630 saw numerically: residues 2,4 give 25U and nonresidues 3,5,6 give 18U.  The all-equal a=1 packet cancels.

============================================================================================
4+1+1 PACKET: (1,1,1,1,a,b)
============================================================================================
The unit two-large 4+1+1 row is even more quantized: every unordered pair a<b in {2,...,6} has signed mass in {0,U,8U}.  The primary HYP-2632 refinement adds the affine zero lane a+b=2 and the selector Q(a,b)=ab*(1+3(a+b))-1 for the high/low split off that lane.

